  "entry": "code/app/demo.py",
  "notes": "Found in a public repository and run by a computer-use agent (batch public-1). Trains a reviewer to judge TESS variable-star candidates. For each case it shows the phase-folded light curve, the per-pixel signal map, key numbers and an automatic checklist. The reviewer answers confirm, doubt or discard, then sees the correct answer, an explanation and where the clue was, and the app keeps calibration statistics, including the P-vs-2P period choice. Data used in the run: example. tree.json is the workflow the agent did and a second agent replayed; run.json says how.",
